.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-SCIM-STATUS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-scim-status - Show directory sync state, last sync and group roles


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team scim status <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the team's directory sync state: the connected directory and its state, the number of directory users, when it last synced and any problem, whether only mapped groups are provisioned, and every directory group with the team role it maps to. Owners, admins and auditors can read it. Use --json for every field.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-scim(1)\fP
